```javascript
// Using spread operator and join
const str = "hello";
const reversed = [...str].reverse().join("");
console.log(reversed); // "olleh"

// Using split, reverse, and join
const str2 = "hello";
const reversed2 = str2.split("").reverse().join("");
console.log(reversed2); // "olleh"

// Using reduce
const str3 = "hello";
const reversed3 = str3.split("").reduce((acc, curr, i) => acc + str3[str3.length - 1 - i], "");
console.log(reversed3); // "olleh"
```

Most common and recommended: spread + reverse + join.
